# Thinkora – Project Overview

**App**: Daily inspiration & habit tracker (quotes, habits, widgets). Package: `com.apachi.thinkora`.

**Stack**: Kotlin, Jetpack Compose (Material3), Clean Architecture + MVVM, Hilt, Room, DataStore, Navigation Compose, Glance widgets, Coroutines/Flow.

**Docs**: `README.md`, `docs/technical.md`, `docs/functional.md`, `docs/status_and_next_steps.md`.

**Structure**:
- `app/` – Application entry, `MainActivity`, NavHost, theme/splash.
- `core/designsystem` – Theme (ThinkoraTheme, Color, Type), shared components (e.g. ThinkoraTopAppBar).
- `core/domain` – Models, repository interfaces, use cases, navigation (`Screen` sealed class).
- `core/data` – Repositories impl, Room DAOs/entities, DataStore, analytics/ads.
- `core/ui` – Shared UI (e.g. HeroQuoteCard, ads).
- `feature/*` – Feature modules: each has Screen(s), ViewModel, optional sub-screens (e.g. `feature/home`, `feature/onboarding`, `feature/main`).

**Conventions**:
- Navigation: `Screen` in `core/domain`; routes like `"screen_name"` or `"screen/{param}"` with `createRoute(param)`.
- ViewModels: `@HiltViewModel`, inject use cases; expose single `State` (data class) and `onEvent(Event)`.
- UI: Prefer `core/designsystem` and `MaterialTheme`; avoid hardcoded colors/strings where theme/strings exist.

**Imports (important)**: Never use fully qualified names inside the code body. Always declare imports at the top of the file and use short names in composables and elsewhere.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD – FQN inside code
composable(com.apachi.thinkora.domain.navigation.Screen.MainScreen.route) { ... }
val vm: com.apachi.thinkora.feature.onboarding.OnboardingViewModel = hiltViewModel(parentEntry)

// ✅ GOOD – imports at top, short names in code
import com.apachi.thinkora.domain.navigation.Screen
import com.apachi.thinkora.feature.onboarding.OnboardingViewModel
// ...
composable(Screen.MainScreen.route) { ... }
val vm: OnboardingViewModel = hiltViewModel(parentEntry)
```
